{
  "$comment": "SCP-OUT-031 \u00a75.4.4 OutletError cross-SDK conformance fixtures. Generated from the registry (crates/scp-protocol/src/context/outlets/error_codes.rs). The Rust conformance gate set-equates fixture coverage against the registry's ALL_SLUGS array (and pins each pair to the pub CODE_*/SLUG_* constants), so a slug added to the registry without a fixture here FAILS the gate by construction. `fixtures` holds one VALID descriptor per (code, slug) pair covering every \u00a75.4.4 slug and every allocated code; each carries a valid per-class DetailBody shape. These fixtures establish the STRUCTURAL / field-level contract (class, code, slug, retry, detail shape, field widths) \u2014 NOT golden serialized wire bytes: `message` is a TEST-ONLY plaintext stand-in for the SDK's reconstructed developer-facing catalog message; the real on-wire tag-4 field is HMAC-SHA-256(outlet_message_key, catalog_key)[..32], never prose. Golden serialized-envelope bytes + the expected HMAC value per fixture are a PR-2 deliverable (once the bridge wire format is settled); until then SDK round-trip means reconstructing the typed envelope from the descriptor, not deserializing a wire blob. One fixture embeds an email + DID to exercise the AC9/AC10 redactor. `pad_nonce` (16-byte hex) and `registration_event_id` (32-byte hex) are emitted unconditionally per \u00a75.4.4 round-5/6. `malformed` holds one detail-shape mismatch per class (detail.kind() != class.expected_detail()) for the per-SDK AC10 rejection tests. `supplementary` holds the top cross-SDK round-trip hazards (a 32-byte ExecutionPanic hash; a >2^53 u64). Neither `malformed` nor `supplementary` counts toward the per-(code,slug) coverage. The Rust gate is crates/scp-testing/tests/integration/outlet_error_conformance.rs.",
